# Parameters

The ROM was designed using parameters so that its size can be changed without rewriting the entire module.

The important parameters are:

- ADDR_WIDTH
- DATA_WIDTH

The memory depth is determined by the address width:

Depth = 2^ADDR_WIDTH

This makes the design more reusable and introduces the type of parameterization that will become useful in larger hardware systems.

